		<text x="544" y="58" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#0f172a">JetStream (/data)</text>
		<text x="544" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">WorkQueue Streams</text>
		<text x="544" y="94" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#475569">KV Buckets (KV_*)</text>
	</svg>
}

templ natsCoreGuide() {
	@docH2("subjects", "Subjects and wildcards")
	@docP() {
		Core NATS routes messages by dot-delimited subjects such as @docCodeWord("pricing.quote.us")&#46; Subscribers match one token with @docCodeWord("*") or any trailing tokens with @docCodeWord(">")&#46; Delivery is at-most-once: if no subscriber is listening when a message is published, NATS drops it immediately.
	}
	@docH2("queues", "Queue groups")
	@docP() {
		When multiple replicas subscribe with the same queue group name, NATS delivers each matching message to exactly one member of the group — giving you instant, location-transparent load balancing with zero broker configuration.
	}
	@docH2("reqreply", "Request-reply RPC")
	@docP() {
		Calling @docCodeWord("nc.Request(subject, data, timeout)") creates a unique ephemeral inbox subject, publishes the request with that reply-to address, and waits for the first responder to call @docCodeWord("m.Respond")&#46;
	}
	@docCode("core.go", natsCoreCode)
}

templ natsWorkQueueGuide() {
	@docH2("workqueue", "WorkQueue retention vs Kafka")
	@docP() {
		In Kafka, consumers move a partition offset forward while historical messages remain on disk until retention expires. A JetStream stream with @docCodeWord("WorkQueuePolicy") behaves like a true durable queue: each message is delivered to a single consumer and deleted from the stream the instant it is acknowledged.
	}
	@docH2("pull", "Durable pull consumers")
	@docP() {
		Worker replicas share one durable pull consumer and call @docCodeWord("cons.Fetch") at their own pace, naturally providing backpressure without overwhelming slow workers.
	}
	@docH2("retries", "Ack, NakWithDelay, and MaxDeliver")
	@docP() {
		Call @docCodeWord("msg.Ack()") after work succeeds, or @docCodeWord("msg.NakWithDelay(d)") to schedule a retry on transient failures. If a worker crashes before acknowledging, JetStream automatically redelivers after @docCodeWord("AckWait") up to @docCodeWord("MaxDeliver") attempts.
	}
	@docCode("workqueue.go", natsWorkQueueCode)
}

templ natsKVGuide() {
	@docH2("buckets", "KV buckets on JetStream")
	@docP() {
		A JetStream Key-Value bucket is backed by a compacted stream named @docCodeWord("KV_<bucket>")&#46; Setting @docCodeWord("History: 5") keeps the last 5 revisions of every key so you can audit changes or roll back.
	}
	@docH2("cas", "Optimistic concurrency with Update")
	@docP() {
		Every write increments a monotonic revision number. Using @docCodeWord("kv.Update(ctx, key, val, expectedRevision)") performs a compare-and-swap on the server and rejects conflicting writes with an error when another writer updated the key first.
	}
	@docH2("watch", "Reactive Watch without polling")
	@docP() {
		Subscribers call @docCodeWord("kv.WatchAll(ctx)") or watch a wildcard such as @docCodeWord("flags.>") to receive initial snapshots followed by real-time updates and deletes over the existing TLS connection.
	}
	@docCode("kv.go", natsKVCode)
}

templ natsInBreadboardGuide() {
	@docH2("tls", "TLS and token auth")
	@docP() {
		Breadboard runs @docCodeWord("nats:2.15.3-alpine3.22") with TLS mandatory on client port @docCodeWord("4222") using the service's lab certificate and token auth supplied via @docCodeWord("--auth") so @docCodeWord("nats.conf") stays secret-free. Monitoring stays strictly on @docCodeWord("127.0.0.1:8222") inside the container.
	}
	@docCode("experiment.yaml", natsSpecYAML)
	@docH2("env", "What your app receives")
	@docP() {
		Apps with @docCodeWord("nats") in @docCodeWord("uses") receive @docCodeWord("NATS_URL")&#44; @docCodeWord("NATS_TOKEN")&#44; and @docCodeWord("NATS_CA") — plus @docCodeWord("SSL_CERT_FILE") automatically:
	}
	@docCode("connect.go", natsConnectCode)
	@docH2("explore", "The Streams & stats tab")
	@docP() {
		Open the NATS service page in @docCodeWord("bb serve") and switch to <strong>Streams &amp; stats</strong> (or call the @docCodeWord("nats_overview") MCP tool) to inspect live connections, message counters, JetStream streams, KV buckets, and consumer pending/ack-pending counts.
	}
}
